    >>> a @ a @ a  # equivalent evaluated directly
    Array([[ 37.,  54.],
           [ 81., 118.]], dtype=float32)

    This also supports zero powers:

    >>> jnp.linalg.matrix_power(a, 0)
    Array([[1., 0.],
           [0., 1.]], dtype=float32)

